{
  "note": "Intake packet rev 5 section 8 (pre-registered 2026-11-15) and [V2.71], [V2.73] (2026-11-16): the chain-eval shapes, verbatim; each must-veto shape's reach is the scripted first Decision of its reach arm and names the judge it measures (intake: an insufficient value or state set; audit: a set the intake check does not cover, or covers rightly, that code can prove); intake_truth is whether a declared set finishes the request, keyed by closing kind and the param's words per subgoal in order (kind:words, comma-joined; a state subgoal declares its wanted state, so its kind is state=<wanted>; a value subgoal declares its field, so its kind is value=<field words> or value=unnamed, [V2.84]); a set not named is unknown; wrong_field is [V2.72]'s right words in the wrong field, restructured by [V2.84]: a set that declares unnamed while the request names a field is insufficient (the intake must veto, the audit must veto under forced allow); a declared field on the wrong element is a code test, not a shape. [V2.79]: request, page, oracle, intake_truth and the scripted arms are templates: {v} (and {email}) take the drawn pool value, {d1} and {d2} the next two pool values (the page's other options); pools hold at least 20 values and a held-out pool shares none with the gate shapes.",
